INT. AMBULANCE - PARADE ROUTE - DAY

Siren off. Confetti on the windshield. A marching band thumps outside. The rig is parked in a crowd.

PARAMEDIC LUCIANA ORTEGA (30s, ponytail) kneels over a MAN on the gurney. He is gray, gasping. PARAMEDIC FITZGERALD "FITZ" BOYLE (50s, mustache) shoves an oxygen mask over his face. INTERN SUNITA RAO (20s, first week) clutches the monitor. DRIVER MOSES BELL (40s, hi-vis vest) leans in from the front seat. A bystander, MRS. DELACROIX-NGUYEN (70s, parade sash), clambers in uninvited. A SON, JOON-HO KANG (20s, shaking), hovers at the rear doors.

LUCIANA
Fitz, line, now.

FITZ
Doing it, Lu.

SUNITA
Pressure's ninety over fifty!

MOSES
Do I roll?

MRS. DELACROIX-NGUYEN
He's my neighbor! He sings in the choir!

LUCIANA
Ma'am, out.

JOON-HO
Dad! Dad, look at me!

FITZ
Joon-ho, back up, give her room.

SUNITA
Eighty over forty!

LUCIANA
Push epi. Sunita, you push it.

SUNITA
Me?

LUCIANA
You.

Sunita takes the syringe. Her hand trembles. Fitz steadies her wrist.

FITZ
Easy, kid. Slow.

She pushes. Everyone holds still. The band outside blares a brass chord.

The monitor beeps. Beeps again. Settles into a rhythm.

SUNITA
Ninety-five over sixty.

MOSES
Moses is rolling.

Luciana sits back on her heels and exhales. Mrs. Delacroix-Nguyen crosses herself. Joon-ho grips the rail.

JOON-HO
Is he okay?

LUCIANA
He's coming back, Joon-ho. You did good.

FITZ
Sunita did good.

SUNITA
(shaking, grinning)
I did good?

LUCIANA
You did good, rookie.

Moses pulls out. The crowd parts. A tuba player salutes.
